WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.862
After calculating a numeric quality score, we can summarize records into categories.

00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:15.507
The query creates score bands such as Excellent, Good, Fair, and Poor, and then counts how many customers fall into each

00:00:15.507 --> 00:00:18.874
band. This can make a quality report easier to read.

00:00:19.442 --> 00:00:23.619
But be careful not to hide too much information behind a label.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:28.064
Suppose two customers both receive a score of seventy-five.

00:00:28.064 --> 00:00:33.499
One may be missing a phone number, while the other may have an invalid email.

00:00:33.499 --> 00:00:37.774
They have the same total score but different problems.

00:00:37.774 --> 00:00:45.814
So quality bands are useful for high-level summaries, while the detailed issue flags remain important for action.

00:00:45.814 --> 00:00:52.295
Use summaries to communicate. Use component-level checks to diagnose and improve the data.
